# No longer provisional. Grounded in "Intro Focus 25" (Wave VII - Voyager,
# CD2-3): the tape passes through Focus 24 on the way from 23 to 25 and
# describes it only as a passage -- a point of light growing larger and
# brighter, familiar, until it's large enough to move into. Thin, but real:
# the tape's own account, not a placeholder. Same automated-scanner caveat as
# briefing-f22.gws -- Library.sourceCoverage() still reads 0 here because the
# tape never pairs "focus" directly next to the digits.

@segment     briefing-f24
@title       Focus 24 — The Approaching Light
@levels      F24
@duration    ~30s

say You are now in Focus 24.
pause 5
say Ahead of you, a point of light. It's growing larger as you move toward it -- bright, but familiar, the kind of bright you get used to.
pause 8
say The light is large enough now to move into. When you're ready, continue forward.
pause 8
